"### Income streams \u2014 how diversified is the cash flow?\n\nAnnualised, blended run-rate \u2248 **$1.35B**:\n- **Core crypto perp fees** $1.04B (77%) \u2014 the engine; pure crypto-trading beta.\n- **Builder/RWA fees (est)** $17.15M (1%) \u2014 HIP-3 equity/commodity perps at ~0.6 bps 'growth-mode' take; **graduating** these to standard rates (~2+ bps) is the biggest single upside lever, and it's non-crypto-correlated.\n- **Spot fees** $30.79M (2%).\n- **USDC collateral yield (est)** $264.53M (20%) \u2014 ~4.3% on \u2248$6.87B of collateral. **Rate-sensitive**: a Fed cutting cycle shrinks this stream even if volume holds (the Coinbase/USDC deal made it structural).\n\n**Takeaway:** today it's ~crypto-perp-dominated, but the two fastest-growing streams (RWA fees, collateral yield) are **not** crypto-beta \u2014 which is exactly what would de-risk the valuation in a crypto bear.\n\n<sub>Core/spot from DefiLlama fees (live). Builder fees = live builder volume \u00d7 est take; collateral yield = DefiLlama TVL \u00d7 live 3M T-bill (FRED). Estimates flagged \u2014 tune the take-rate/haircut in `hype.py`.</sub>"